[p112]       4.2.    BUILD-002 Pricing Action Definition
[p112] 
[p112] 
[p112] Users must be able to define the pricing action they are constructing.
[p112] 
[p112] Supported actions should include:
[p112] 
[p112]    ● set a new price;
[p112]    ● increase price;
[p112]    ● decrease price;
[p112]    ● apply a percentage adjustment;
[p112]    ● apply an absolute-value adjustment;
[p112] 
[p113]     ● maintain or protect a target margin;
[p113]     ● apply a markup;
[p113]     ● establish promotional pricing;
[p113]     ● markdown pricing;
[p113]     ● create pricing for a new product or service;
[p113]     ● define or modify a pricing rule;
[p113]     ● define a custom pricing action using supported builder components.
[p113] 
[p113] Quantitative pricing actions covered by ANALYSIS-002 must use the deterministic
[p113] calculation definitions established in Section 3.5 where the required inputs are available.
[p113] 
[p113] New-product or service pricing, pricing rules and custom pricing actions may contain
[p113] structured elements that are not themselves deterministically calculable.
[p113] 
[p113] The Builder must not represent a pricing outcome as deterministically calculated unless the
[p113] required inputs, operators and calculation method are supported by the analytical calculation
[p113] layer.
[p113] 
[p113] Where part of a pricing action depends on qualitative judgement, unsupported logic or a
[p113] manually determined commercial value, that component must remain distinguishable from
[p113] system-calculated quantitative output.
[p113] 
[p113]

[p122]     4.19.     BUILD-019 AI-Assisted Construction
