[p126] 
[p126] For pricing work that contains non-deterministic components, the output must preserve those
[p126] components without falsely converting them into calculated quantitative results.
[p126] 
[p126] The Builder output must provide sufficient information for:
[p126] 
[p126]    ● pricing analysis;
[p126]    ● Scenario evaluation;
[p126]    ● collaboration;
[p126]    ● review;
[p126]    ● Pricing Proposal creation;
[p126]    ● organisational decision;
[p126]    ● execution preparation;
[p126]    ● historical understanding.
[p126] 
[p126] The Pricing Builder therefore serves as the controlled bridge between a business pricing
[p126] objective and the specific pricing action ultimately submitted for organisational decision.
